# Architecture

## Component Hierarchy

```
App → QueryClientProvider → OrderbookWidget
  → Header (SymbolSelector, PrecisionSelector)
  → ConnectionStatus
  → Orderbook → AsksTable, SpreadDisplay, BidsTable
    → OrderbookSide → OrderbookRow (+ DepthBar)
```

## Data Flow

- **useOrderbookSocket(coin, precisionLevel)**: Opens one WebSocket; subscribes to l2Book with params from `precisionLevelToSubscription(precisionLevel)` (nSigFigs + optional mantissa). Parses messages, writes to cache via `queryClient.setQueryData(queryKeys.orderbook(coin, precisionLevel), processed)` and `queryKeys.connection`. On coin/precision change: unsubscribe then subscribe on the same socket; new connection only on disconnect/reconnect.
- **useOrderbook(coin, precisionLevel)**: `useQuery` with same key; components read from cache. No HTTP `queryFn`; WebSocket is source of truth.
- **useConnection()**: Consumes `queryKeys.connection` for status.

## File Layout (PRD Section 13)

- `components/OrderbookWidget.tsx` — container; owns coin and precisionLevel state.
- `components/Orderbook/` — Orderbook, OrderbookSide, OrderbookRow, DepthBar, SpreadDisplay.
- `components/Controls/` — SymbolSelector, PrecisionSelector.
- `hooks/useOrderbookSocket.ts`, `useOrderbook.ts`, `useConnection.ts`.
- `lib/orderbook.ts` — `processOrderbookData`; `lib/queryClient.ts` — client config.
- `types/index.ts` — all shared types and `queryKeys`. Add new types there.

Keep new code in these modules; do not introduce parallel hierarchies or duplicate query key logic.
